From e97ee144d9c5aa041f04b67262c5f59a4fa8478c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:49:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Air battle sound: the master limiter's detector digital
 with 5 ms look-ahead (a transient got 1.5 dB past the ceiling)

The ground scene's second film measured one transient 1.5 dB past the -1.5 dB ceiling for 1.3 ms with the
engine's default analog detector and 3 ms of look-ahead. The air battle builds the same limiter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhz35oCkUv94Xb2EwCjp
---
 unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json            | 5 +++--
 .../Source/TheaterCommand/Battle/AirBattle.cpp               | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json b/unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json
index 7fdb5d2b..5fc8b170 100644
--- a/unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json
+++ b/unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 {
   "what": "The battle mix: how every approved battle sound is blended by unit, distance and how hot the fight is, so a battle plays like a war film. Numbers are the sound director's to tune; the 3D game reads them. Spec in plain words: battle-mix.md beside this file.",
   "version": 5,
-  "changes": "v5 (21 Nov, release 2; the 3D game's second air sound patch, sound/air-r2/): rounds striking a plane (air.roundsHit, silent until Brian marks round seven's hits Good); close flak in every view (air.closeView.closeFlak); big moments dip the rest in the air battle (big, air.bigDuck); dead engines thin the drones (air.engineLost); the battle's music driven by the air battle's own meter (music._air). Land (the ground battle sound thread): a new top-level `land` block, which touches no existing row. No number changed. v4's changes: mix-v4.json beside this file. After the review (21 Nov, 19:40Z), no number changed: air.roundsPassing.reach (new, 1000 m: rounds crack past beyond the guns' convergence); a fighter's fixed guns of one kind are one take (air.gunsByCalibre._wing); close flak is always heard (air.closeView.closeFlak._always); formation loops in air.loopsFamily, as written here; the master limiter's knee hard (buses.master._knee). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:25Z by the ground sound thread: land.mgClose.endFade 0.04 replaces tail, tailFade and farTail, and land.cracks.runFade 0.04 replaces runTail (the MG recordings fire on after a burst's last round, so the 0.3 s tail was about eight more rounds at full level). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:36Z by the ground sound thread: land.garand.reloadFromClips and reloadPieces (the reload heard from the clip recordings), and land.smgCue (the squad leader's Thompson burst, MP 38 takes standing in until a real Thompson is recorded). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:39Z by the ground sound thread: land.smgCue.leaderRoles (officer, leader), and the Garand reload and the leader's Thompson switch on by themselves at the first clip cue (notes only; the code default matches).",
+  "changes": "v5 (21 Nov, release 2; the 3D game's second air sound patch, sound/air-r2/): rounds striking a plane (air.roundsHit, silent until Brian marks round seven's hits Good); close flak in every view (air.closeView.closeFlak); big moments dip the rest in the air battle (big, air.bigDuck); dead engines thin the drones (air.engineLost); the battle's music driven by the air battle's own meter (music._air). Land (the ground battle sound thread): a new top-level `land` block, which touches no existing row. No number changed. v4's changes: mix-v4.json beside this file. After the review (21 Nov, 19:40Z), no number changed: air.roundsPassing.reach (new, 1000 m: rounds crack past beyond the guns' convergence); a fighter's fixed guns of one kind are one take (air.gunsByCalibre._wing); close flak is always heard (air.closeView.closeFlak._always); formation loops in air.loopsFamily, as written here; the master limiter's knee hard (buses.master._knee). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:25Z by the ground sound thread: land.mgClose.endFade 0.04 replaces tail, tailFade and farTail, and land.cracks.runFade 0.04 replaces runTail (the MG recordings fire on after a burst's last round, so the 0.3 s tail was about eight more rounds at full level). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:36Z by the ground sound thread: land.garand.reloadFromClips and reloadPieces (the reload heard from the clip recordings), and land.smgCue (the squad leader's Thompson burst, MP 38 takes standing in until a real Thompson is recorded). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:39Z by the ground sound thread: land.smgCue.leaderRoles (officer, leader), and the Garand reload and the leader's Thompson switch on by themselves at the first clip cue (notes only; the code default matches). The master limiter's detector (21 Nov 19:50Z): digital, 5 ms look-ahead (buses.master._detector); no number changed.",
   "made": "2026-11-21",
   "files": "/mnt/project-files/sound/battle-pack/wav/",
   "units": "metres of the battlefield (the sims' x, y), seconds, decibels. 0 dB = the file as made.",
@@ -30,7 +30,8 @@
       "limiterCeilingDb": -1.5,
       "limiterReleaseMs": 120,
       "note": "a limiter on the whole battle so stacked blasts never clip. v3: ceiling -1.5 because the limiter works on samples (as UE's submix limiter does) and between samples the air battle's close view reached -0.8 dBTP; -1.5 keeps the true peak under -1. If the engine's limiter looks between samples, -1.0 dBTP instead",
-      "_knee": "the limiter's knee is hard (0 dB): the engine's default 10 dB knee began pressing 5 dB under the ceiling"
+      "_knee": "the limiter's knee is hard (0 dB): the engine's default 10 dB knee began pressing 5 dB under the ceiling",
+      "_detector": "the limiter's detector is digital (bAnalogMode off) with 5 ms of look-ahead: the engine's default analog detector with 3 ms let a transient 1.5 dB past the ceiling for 1.3 ms (the ground scene's second film, part 3 at 36.5 s, measured by the ground sound thread)"
     }
   },
   "distance": {
diff --git a/unreal/TheaterCommand/Source/TheaterCommand/Battle/AirBattle.cpp b/unreal/TheaterCommand/Source/TheaterCommand/Battle/AirBattle.cpp
index d5d97b7f..d9a2896e 100644
--- a/unreal/TheaterCommand/Source/TheaterCommand/Battle/AirBattle.cpp
+++ b/unreal/TheaterCommand/Source/TheaterCommand/Battle/AirBattle.cpp
@@ -556,7 +556,10 @@ bool AAirBattle::Open(const FString& Why)
 			Settings.DynamicsProcessorType = ESubmixEffectDynamicsProcessorType::Limiter;
 			Settings.PeakMode = ESubmixEffectDynamicsPeakMode::Peak;
 			Settings.ThresholdDb = static_cast<float>(AirParts::MixNumber(Mix, TEXT("buses.master.limiterCeilingDb"), -1.5));
-			Settings.LookAheadMsec = 3.0f;
+			// (a digital detector with 5 ms of look-ahead: the engine's default analog detector at 3 ms let a
+			// transient 1.5 dB past the ceiling for 1.3 ms in the ground scene's second film, the same limiter)
+			Settings.bAnalogMode = false;
+			Settings.LookAheadMsec = 5.0f;
 			Settings.AttackTimeMsec = 1.0f;
 			Settings.ReleaseTimeMsec = static_cast<float>(AirParts::MixNumber(Mix, TEXT("buses.master.limiterReleaseMs"), 120.0));
 			Settings.InputGainDb = 0.0f;
-- 
